# handoff docs (HO 604). These were already ignored per-machine via
# core.excludesFile (~/.gitignore_global), so they never reach the repo and a
# deploy never sees them. Repeating it HERE is what stops Tailwind reading them:
# the v4 scanner honours a repo .gitignore but NOT core.excludesFile, so on this
# machine it was compiling class names out of handoff PROSE — `text-[10px]`,
# and a literal `text-[length:var(--fs-N)]` off a line of spec text. Those rules
# existed only in local builds, never in the deployed bundle, which is the
# problem: the local build compiled from inputs the deploy does not have. This
# line restores build-input parity and makes a fresh clone behave like this
# machine without needing the global ignore.
docs/handoffs/
